<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>Why<sp/>this<sp/>chapter</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Sattyre<sp/>starts<sp/>with<sp/>a<sp/>build<sp/>system<sp/>that<sp/>fails<sp/>clearly<sp/>and<sp/>enables<sp/>optional<sp/>subsystems<sp/>deliberately.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">This<sp/>chapter<sp/>focuses<sp/>on<sp/>CMake<sp/>options<sp/>and<sp/>directory<sp/>ownership<sp/>so<sp/>contributors<sp/>do<sp/>not<sp/>blur<sp/>boundaries.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>goal<sp/>is<sp/>a<sp/>stable<sp/>developer<sp/>baseline<sp/>before<sp/>touching<sp/>parser,<sp/>solver,<sp/>plugin,<sp/>or<sp/>packaging<sp/>internals.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">```text</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cmake<sp/>-S<sp/>.<sp/>-B<sp/>build/default<sp/>-DSATTYRE_ENABLE_TESTS=ON</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cmake<sp/>--build<sp/>build/default<sp/>-j</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ctest<sp/>--test-dir<sp/>build/default<sp/>--output-on-failure</highlight></codeline>
